# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent tooling, research working files, and source dumps.
#
# These are the inputs and scratch notes behind the site, not the site itself.
# They are kept locally on purpose — .research/ holds the raw GitHub API dump
# and the compiled findings that data/*.ts was written from, and losing them
# means re-running the research. They just should not be in a public repo.
#
# NOTE: git does not track empty directories, and `git rm --cached` is needed
# for anything already committed — adding a line here does not untrack a file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Claude Code / agent harness
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.mcp.json
.cursor/
.aider*
.windsurf/

# research + source dumps that fed data/*.ts
.research/
spec.md
linkdin.md
linkedin.md
mohnish.txt

# The previous Vite site. Kept locally as the content reference this rebuild
# was written from — the skills list, the career entries and the school results
# all came out of it. Not built, not deployed, and not something a public repo
# should carry a second copy of.
website/

# local-only documentation — working docs, not repo docs.
# README.md is the only documentation that ships.
HOW_TO_USE.md
architecture.md
tasks.md

# Source documents dropped in the repo root: CVs, transcripts, anything that
# was being read from while editing. This repo is public and its contents are
# downloadable by anyone, so a CV sitting here is a phone number and an address
# published by accident.
#
# The leading slash confines this to the root on purpose. public/resume.pdf is
# still committable, because that one is published deliberately and is what
# siteConfig.resumeAvailable turns on.
/*.pdf

# scratch
*.local
.scratch/
tmp/
